## Local development

One-time, one connection store (`st.connection("snowflake")` reads the `snow` CLI's
default connection locally, so nothing is typed twice):

```bash
uv tool install streamsnow snowflake-cli pre-commit
snow connection add --connection-name {{ connection_name }} --account {{ account }} \
  --user <you> --authenticator externalbrowser --default
pre-commit install                                  # the governance hooks
```

{% set slug = app_slug or '<slug>' %}
Per app:

```bash
{% if runtime == 'container' %}
uv venv --python {{ container_python }} && uv pip install -e apps/{{ slug }}   # the app's pyproject.toml deps, in .venv
{% else %}
uv venv --python 3.11                               # then install environment.yml's packages:
uv pip install streamlit pandas plotly snowflake-snowpark-python   # match the pins in apps/{{ slug }}/environment.yml
{% endif %}
streamsnow validate-app {{ slug }}                # PASS/FAIL gate
streamsnow preview {{ slug }}                     # runs .venv/bin/streamlit against live Snowflake
```

{% if runtime == 'warehouse' %}
Warehouse apps have no `pyproject.toml` (Snowflake installs `environment.yml` from its
Anaconda channel), so `uv pip install -e` does not apply; if `streamlit` is missing,
`streamsnow preview` prints the exact install line for the app.

{% endif %}
{% if app_slug %}
The starter page renders sample numbers, and `queries/example_metric.sql` (plus the
review window in `sql_review/index.yaml`) reads `YOUR_TABLE`. Replace all three with
real content, or repoint them at a real table in an allowed schema: `validate-app`
fails while any app file still reads `YOUR_TABLE`, so the placeholder app cannot
ship. The first real query is the first real Snowflake round-trip. `apps/{{ app_slug }}/.streamlit/secrets.toml` (gitignored) is an
optional override for an app that needs a different role or warehouse.
{% else %}
`apps/<slug>/.streamlit/secrets.toml` (gitignored) is an optional override for an app
that needs a different role or warehouse.
{% endif %}

## Add an app

```bash
streamsnow new <domain> <function>
```

Governance rules (data access, caching, SQL layout, deploy) live in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md).
Configuration is in [`streamsnow.config.yaml`](streamsnow.config.yaml).
